\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Swoons,MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected;Bonds Soft   \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2007\par 10:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.5364   +0.0060 \par    Overnight rate        2.44     unch \par    Two-year bond yield:  2.24     +2 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.87     +1 bp \par    Two-year swap offer:  2.96     +6 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   3.27     -5 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   31 bps   -11 bps \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar tumbled Thursday amid a worldwide sell-off in emerging markets, prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and offer the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a cushion, according to traders.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The greenback traded as high as S$1.5402, and traders said The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore bought about S$200 million in Singapore dollars to absorb the impact of capital outflows.   \par \par \uc2 One trader told Dow Jones Newswires that the MAS bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the morning as the U.S. dollar rose from S$1.5320 to S$1.5400.   \par \par \uc2 A second trader said the MAS entered the market both Wednesday and Thursday to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has declined about 1.5% against the greenback since Monday.   \par \par \uc2 The MAS and other central banks in Asia have a history of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the region faced a meltdown in 1997.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said Malaysia's Bank Negara was also active Thursday, and Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both countries touched multi-month lows.   \par \par \uc2 Analytical models show the trade-weighted Singapore dollar is well within the confines of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's secret policy band, suggesting the MAS may act to smooth but not stop further losses in the near term.   \par \par \uc2 In the government bond market, short-dated paper was soft as banks were reluctant to loan cash and the overnight rate temporarily spiked.   \par \par \uc2 Two traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added about S$100 million to Singapore's money market Thursday after withdrawing cash Tuesday and Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The modest injection suggests that Singapore isn't yet facing a severe liquidity squeeze.   \par \par \uc2 "The MAS realizes it doesn't need to add substantial liquidity at this point even though the overnight rate has come up," one trader said. "Banks have the cash but they're just holding on to it - that's what's pushing rates higher."   \par \par \uc2 The overnight deposit rate rose as high as 3.00% from 2.44% Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "They're willing to add liquidity but right now it's not needed," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4153; john.jannarone@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Roger Ng [ 16-08-07 0848GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070816e38g000df\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
