r \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the greenback would have to reach S$1.4767 to breach to band's top. \par   But UOB also expects near-term psychological resistance to be a factor. \par   'Key support for the (U.S. dollar) is likely to hold at S$1.5100,' the bank said in a note to clients. \par   Singapore government bonds rose after two losing sessions, yet again defying U.S. Treasurys. \par   '(U.S.) Treasurys were down, but the market has a mind of its own at this point,' a local fixed-income trader said. \par   He said that speculators had driven interest rate swap levels higher earlier in the week and that bond yields had risen in synch. \par    'Yields were artificially propped,' he said. 'There was room for retracement.' \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4152; john.jannarone@dowjones.com -0-    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070720e37k006hf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
