\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Flat Late But Vulnerable; Bonds Edge Lower   \b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2007\par 10:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                        Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD               1.5300   +0.0005 \par  Overnight Rate        1.75%    -19 bps \par  Two-Year Bond Yield:  2.30%    +1 bp \par  10-Year Bond Yield:   2.90%    +2 bps \par  Two-Year Swap Offer:  2.86%    +3 bps \par  10-Year Swap Offer:   3.33%    +2 bps \par  2-10-Yr Swap Curve:   47 bps   -1 bp \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was steady in Asia Wednesday, but traders say the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is exposed to a spillover effect if the Malaysian ringgit continues to fall.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 "The Malaysian ringgit has trended weaker, and the Singapore dollar would follow if (the ringgit) has a major breakout," a trader said.   \par \par \uc2 "If the U.S. dollar moves much beyond MYR3.4200 the Singapore dollar could break out of its range as well."   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar has traded in a tight band between S$1.5280 and S$1.5320 this week, but simultaneously climbed against the ringgit to about MYR3.4200 from MYR3.4000.   \par \par \uc2 If the Singapore dollar does decline in coming sessions, traders don't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "No one is talking about the (\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) right now," another trader said.   \par \par \uc2 "We're a long way from the point where the MAS would come in."   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses exchange-rate targeting as its chief policy tool and currently advocates a modest appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed, trade-weighted band.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the Singapore dollar has recently fallen beneath the midpoint of the secret band after clinging near its ceiling through much of last year and early last year.   \par \par \uc2 Local bonds fell in tandem with a decline in U.S. Treasurys overnight, and late-dated issues may suffer most if selling continues.   \par \par \uc2 "The move today reflected U.S. Treasurys," said Enrico Tanuwidjaja, a strategist at OCBC.   \par \par \uc2 "If there's more selling, we should see some steepening going on for the next few sessions."   \par \par \uc2 The flush money market has lent support to short-dated issues in recent months, but last week's auction of 10-year government bonds suggested a weaker appetite for longer-term paper.   \par \par \uc2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4152; john.jannarone@dowjones.com [ 06-06-07 0839GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070606e366000e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
