\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Flat; Yield Curve Steeper On 3-Month Auction   \b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2007\par 10:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                 1.5125   unch \par  Overnight Deposit Rate  2.31%    +12 bps \par  Two-Year Bond Yield:    2.26%    unch \par  10-Year Bond Yield:     2.70%    +4 bps \par  Two-Year Swap Offer:    2.75%    +2 bps \par  10-Year  Swap Offer:    3.13%    +2 bps \par  2-10-Year Swap Curve:   38 bps   unch \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was flat in Asia Monday, and although estimates suggest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been slow to rise as traders remain guarded.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 "For now, there is still room for the (Singapore dollar) to strengthen further without challenging the policy threshold,"  \uc2 United Overseas Bank\uc2  said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 UOB estimates that if the Singapore dollar holds steady against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the greenback would need to reach S$1.5050 to prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore uses the exchange rate as its primary policy tool and manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed, trade-weighted band.   \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar dipped below S$1.5100 Friday but the market's a bit jittery and there's been some short covering," a trader at a foreign bank said.   \par \par \uc2 Another trader said that when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last apparently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 12, the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was below the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band's upper limit.   \par \par \uc2 "Since they came in unpredictably before, we think they want to keep the market guessing, so the U.S. dollar may have a hard time breaking S$1.5100," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The trader added that the greenback may encounter a short-term ceiling between S$1.5130 and S$1.5140, a level it remained beneath late last week.   \par \par \uc2 In the government debt market, the yield curve steepened as strong demand in a T-bill auction resulted in the lowest yield in over 18 months.   \par \par \uc2 A S$1.9 billion auction of three-month government T-bills priced at a cutoff yield of 1.94%, the lowest level since September 2005.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign purchases of Singapore dollars have lifted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the top of the secret trading band in recent months, and analysts say the inflows have given government paper a major boost.   \par \par \uc2 "It's still a capital inflows story," said Selena Ling, a fixed-income strategist at OCBC.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers say the MAS historically conducted money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep short-term rates stable, but it's been notably absent in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Singapore benefits from external price competition, and a very low inflation rate has also been a prop for fixed-income assets.   \par \par \uc2 Singapore's consumer prices rose just 0.7% from a year earlier in March, similar to the 0.6% rise in February.   \par \par \uc2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4152; john.jannarone@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 23-04-07 0814GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070423e34n000hn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\p