\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Flat;Bonds Take Breather After Week Of Gains   \b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2007\par 11:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                 1.5125   -0.0005 \par  Overnight Deposit Rate  2.19%    +31 bps \par  Two-Year Bond Yield:    2.25%    +3 bps \par  10-Year Bond Yield:     2.66%    +6 bps \par  Two-Year Swap Offer:    2.73%    +7 bps \par  10-Year  Swap Offer:    3.11%    +10 bps \par  2-10-Year Swap Curve:   38 bps   +3 bps \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was flat in Asia Friday, but traders say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will retain a strong bias next week and may challenge a key psychological barrier.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar is heavy, and if we can drop below S$1.5100 it's possible we'll go to S$1.5050 early next week," a trader at a Japanese bank said.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar has edged below the psychologically important S$1.5100 level in recent sessions - touching new 10-year lows - but hasn't made a decisive breakthrough.   \par \par \uc2 The trader said that the Singapore dollar has correlated closely with the Japanese yen recently, and both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to carry momentum Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar did not stay beneath Y118.00, and the S$1.5100 level did not break either," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Traders say that if the Singapore dollar does stage a rally, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels.   \par \par \uc2 "We don't think there's much chance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  coming in here, but we could always get a surprise," another trader said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses the exchange rate as its primary monetary policy tool and manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed, trade-weighted band.   \par \par \uc2 According to  \uc2 United Overseas Bank\uc2 , the U.S. dollar would have to decline to S$1.4982 to lift the trade-weighted basket to the top of the secret \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band.   \par \par \uc2 In the government debt market, bonds fell after a string of recent gains, but investor appetite may return next week as funding costs remain low.   \par \par \uc2 "Given that we have had such a strong week, people may be cautious and probably decided to take some profit off the table," said OCBC strategist Selena Ling.   \par \par \uc2 She said that Singapore's March inflation data, due Monday at 0500 GMT, have the potential to spark a selloff if the figures are much higher than expected.   \par \par \uc2 "If the data come in well above 1.5%, there could be an impact," she said.   \par \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires poll of economists expects consumer prices to have risen 1.0% from a year earlier in March, faster than the 0.6% rise in February.   \par \par \uc2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4152; john.jannarone@dowjones.com [ 20-04-07 0919GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070420e34k000i2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
