\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia up,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears cap rupee's gains   \b0\par\par\uc2 710 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2007\par 05:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , April 18 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose against a weaker dollar on Wednesday, but the Indian rupee retreated amid growing concerns about fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht <THB=TH> gained nearly 0.3 percent to 34.75 to the dollar. It had hit 34.70 in early onshore trading, its highest level in almost a month.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar sank to a 26-year low against sterling <GBP=> and weakened against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after data showing weaker U.S. core consumer inflation in March, bolstered the view that the Federal Reserve may lean towards a rate cut this year.   \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is under pressure. The low consumer prices could be positive for U.S. equities as it helped take some pressure off the Fed, and that was a helpful lead to Asian equity markets," said Sean Callow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Bank.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee <INR=IN> eased back to around 41.95 per dollar surrendering most of its daily gains after briefly hitting 41.80, which was still off its 9-year high of 41.63 hit on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts are concerned that the rupee's rapid gains in recent days might push the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So far they say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to have accepted the strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which helps hold down inflation.   \par \par \uc2  "Following aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February and March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to have scaled back their dollar buying significantly this week," \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists at UBS said in a research note.   \par \par \uc2  The RBI bought $1.14 billion of reserves in the first week of April, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows, implying a slowdown from a record $11.9 billion it bought in February to prevent the rupee's gains.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  LIKELY   \par \par \uc2  But UBS cautioned that the RBI was standing aside to wait for a clearer economic picture, and its dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume if money supply and inflation eased.   \par \par \uc2  "We would therefore not be surprised if the RBI returns to the rupee market before the week is up," UBS said, adding they were cautiously shifting their 1-month dollar/rupee forecast to 42.50.   \par \par \uc2  The won <KRW=> rose as high as 927.3 per dollar, its highest since early January, despite concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Korea, which traders said had stepped into the market this week to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.   \par \par \uc2  The baht has gained about 3.8 percent this year, trailing the rupee's 5.5 percent rise as the best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, despite Bangkok's attempts to cap the baht's rise to protect its exporters.   \par \par \uc2  The government imposed capital controls in December to rein in the baht, but the steps split the market into onshore and offshore segments, with the latter pricing the baht substantially higher at about 32.5 per dollar <THB=W>.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0