\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Gains On Regional Strength; Bonds Lower   \b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2007\par 10:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                 1.5167   -0.0030 \par  Overnight Deposit Rate  2.19%    -6 bps \par  Two-Year Bond Yield:    2.41%    +3 bps \par  10-Year  Bond Yield:    2.76%    +2 bps \par  Two-Year Swap Offer:    2.99%    +2 bps \par  10-Year  Swap Offer:    3.27%    +3 bps \par  2-10-Year Swap Curve:   28 bps   +1 bp \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose in Asian trade Friday on broad strength in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but traders say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may act to block a further rise at any time.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 "A lot of our customers seem willing to sell U.S. dollars whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes in or not," a trader at a foreign bank said. "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't come in, I think the U.S. dollar can keep drifting lower."   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times earlier in the week, driving the U.S. dollar higher in sharp bursts to suppress the local unit's strength.   \par \par \uc2 The trader added that if the MAS doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the greenback may sink to as low as S$1.5140 in the near term before bottoming out.   \par \par \uc2 Another trader said the MAS could enter the market during Friday's European session when volume lightens.   \par \par \uc2 "The MAS has demonstrated it will come in around these levels, and I think it could wait until the market is quieter later in the day," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 In its policy statement Tuesday, the MAS said the trade-weighted Singapore dollar has recently traded near the upper end of its undisclosed policy band.   \par \par \uc2 The MAS uses exchange-rate targeting as its chief policy tool, and since April 2004 has advocated a modest and gradual appreciation of the local unit.   \par \par \uc2 In the local debt market, government bonds edged lower, taking a cue from a modest rise in interest-rate swap levels.   \par \par \uc2 "The IRS market was pulling up, and bond yields followed a bit of the rise," a local trader said.   \par \par \uc2 He added that interest rates in Singapore have reached very low levels, and that a mild adjustment doesn't come as a surprise.   \par \par \uc2 "To see the five-year swap level so close to 3.00% is good enough reason for a little reversal," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the Singapore government to announce the auction size for the May 2 sale of seven-year bonds late next week.   \par \par \uc2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4152; john.jannarone@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 13-04-07 0833GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070413e34d000dv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
