\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr at 3-wk low, mkts wary of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 816 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2007\par 04:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , April 12 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hit a three-week low on Thursday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying of U.S. dollars to cap local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength, while wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped keep other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a tight range.   \par \par \uc2 Markets in the Philippines, Malaysia, South Korea, India as well as \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  have all been watchful this week of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains against a backdrop of firm equities and optimism about economic growth.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) was probably buying U.S. dollars in the market again on Thursday, helping push the Singapore dollar <SGD=> to a three-week trough at 1.5220 per U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar is down about 0.6 percent from Tuesday's 9-1/2-year peak at 1.5110.   \par \par \uc2 "They are getting increasingly frustrated with Sing dollar strength and will increasingly come into the market," said one trader. He thought the MAS had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier from the 1.5170 per dollar level to 1.5220.   \par \par \uc2 The MAS is determined to squeeze out short U.S. dollar    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions against the Singapore dollar -- bets that the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will weaken -- said Tim Condon, head of research at\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ING.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But such trades are likely to remain in favour given that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has just maintained a moderately tight monetary policy, he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The MAS, which uses the exchange rate instead of interest rates to conduct monetary policy, on Tuesday reiterated its stance of allowing "a modest and gradual appreciation" of the trade-weighted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The night before the MAS meeting the Sing dollar was 2.5 percent above the mid-point of its band and very much in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  territory," said Westpac \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Sean Callow, referring to his estimate of the band.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Now it's about 1.9 percent above the mid-point, so \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has helped pull it back."   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WATCHING   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> dipped to the weaker side of 48 per dollar but held near Wednesday's six-year high of 47.90.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but any dollar buying was probably smaller than earlier in the week.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Maybe they were there today and yesterday, but not as actively as they were on Tuesday," said one Manila trader, referring to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In South Korea, the won <KRW=> touched a one-week high at about 931 per dollar amid foreign buying of Korean shares, which hit a fresh record peak. A move to 930 is expected to be met by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , helping to limit won gains.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won also rose to 7.7895 against the yen <JPYKRW=R>, its highest since Feb. 27.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets showed little immediate reaction to a widely expected decision by the Bank of Korea to hold its benchmark interest rate steady at 4.50 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A meeting of the Group of Seven industrial nations, starting on Friday in Washington, helped keep most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  range-bound, dealers said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say the G7 may renew calls for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility in Asia, with a focus on China, to help correct global imbalances.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, the world's largest, rose by $135.7 billion in the first quarter to $1.202 trillon, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Thursday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This could add fresh ammunition to any calls at the G7 meeting for faster appreciation in the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS>, analysts said. China has said top officials will not be attending the G7 meeting.    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0809 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       119.31         119.17       -0.12\par  Sing dlr        1.5193         1.5171       -0.14\par  Taiwan dlr      33.105         33.095       -0.03\par  Korean won      931.50         932.00       +0.05\par  Baht             34.93          34.96       