\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Singapore MAS Keeps Modest, Gradual SGD Rise Policy   \b0\par\par\uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2007\par 02:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from the MAS, influences on the Singapore dollar, growth and inflation outlook.)   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its policy of modest and gradual appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the economy is expected to remain healthy this year and inflation remains low.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore said Tuesday it won't re-center the undisclosed trade-weighted policy band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , nor change the band's slope or width.   \par \par \uc2 All 10 economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires had expected the MAS to maintain the modestly tight policy stance.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the trade-weighted Singapore dollar has fluctuated near the top of its policy band during the last six months.   \par \par \uc2 The MAS operates monetary policy using the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than interest rates, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar within a secret band that market participants estimate.   \par \par \uc2 Strength in the Singapore dollar reflected the broad-based weakness of the U.S. dollar, capital inflows into Asia and the relatively buoyant Singapore economy, the MAS said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 The MAS reiterated its target for economic growth of between 4.5% and 6.5% in 2007, slowing from 7.9% in 2006, and maintained its forecast for full-year inflation to be in a range of 0.5% to 1.5%.   \par \par \uc2 "Looking ahead, the external environment is expected to remain broadly supportive of sustained growth," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2 Growth from Singapore's export sector has moderated but economic activity will be buttressed by the services sector, it said.   \par \par \uc2 Ministry of Trade & Industry figures - also released Tuesday - showed that the Singapore economy slowed in the first quarter but still beat expectations.   \par \par \uc2 On a seasonally adjusted and annualized basis, the economy expanded 7.2% from the fourth quarter, after growing 7.9% in the previous three months. A Dow Jones Newswires poll of economists had forecast a 3.7% expansion.   \par \par \uc2 The MAS said a two-percentage-point increase in the goods and services tax that takes effect in July this year will add 0.5 percentage point to the CPI in 2007 and 2008.   \par \par \uc2 The increase in inflation will be tempered by offsetting fiscal measures and import costs being contained by the stronger Singapore dollar, it said.   \par \par \uc2 -By Singapore Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 10-04-07 0039GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070410e34a00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
