\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Sing dlr retreats from highs,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected   \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2007\par 02:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with latest price move, quote)   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , April 10 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar hit a 9-1/2-year high on Tuesday but then retreated, with dealers suspecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of buying U.S. dollars to curb the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.   \par \par \uc2 By 0345 GMT the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 1.5188 per U.S. dollar, down about 0.5 percent from the peak of 1.5110 hit earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Stronger-than-expected economic growth and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to stick to a policy of modest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation had boosted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "It does feel like they are in but it's hard to be sure," said one trader in Singapore, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Another trader said he suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but not on a large scale.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy grew an annualised 7.2 percent in the first quarter, well above forecasts although a little slower than in the previous quarter.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its policy of a "gradual and modest appreciation" in the Singapore dollar. It uses the exchange rate rather than interest rates to conduct monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 "We were in the minority expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tighten by means of an increase in the slope of the band," Tim Condon, head of research at ING, said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 "We think it's only a matter of time before the MAS tightens, which makes us bearish U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar."   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE-DOLLAR (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070410e34a0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
