\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia powers ahead as Fed modifies tone  \b0\par\par\uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 03:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 22 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended this week's gains on Thursday as the Federal Reserve removed a reference to possible interest rate rises in a policy statement, dealing a blow to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2  However, as the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied, investors grew wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the gains.  \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's ringgit <MYR=> hit a nine-year high at 3.4560 per dollar after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor expressed support for a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose 0.5 percent to a 9-\u189\'00\'BD   year peak at 1.5165 per U.S. dollar, the South Korean won <KRW=> hit a one-month high at about 936 per dollar and the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> jumped 0.8 percent to a three-week high at 9,070 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the Fed left rates steady at 5.25 percent, as expected. But the shift in tone in its policy statement knocked the dollar to a two-year low versus the euro <EUR=>.  \par \par \uc2  The statement also triggered a rally in stocks, helping markets to recover further from the beating they took earlier this month on worries that weakness in the U.S. housing sector could spread to the broader economy.  \par \par \uc2  Asia's stock markets notched up strong gains <.MSCIAPJ>. Tokyo's Nikkei share average <.N225> rose to a three-week high. The high-yielding Australian dollar <AUD=> briefly touched a 10-year peak against the dollar in another sign of a pick up in risk appetite.  \par \par \uc2  "The Fed statement seems to be taken favourably by emerging markets and this is reflected by the weaker yen and stronger Aussie, which is an indication of the return of carry trades," said Bank of America \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Christy Tan.  \par \par \uc2  "This puts Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have been suffering on the rebound."  \par \par \uc2  Asia's high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have seen some of the strongest gains in the region this week. The rupiah, for instance, has risen almost 1.7 percent against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2  SPOTLIGHT ON MALAYSIA  \par \par \uc2  In Kuala Lumpur, an apparent change in the authorities' long-held view of favouring a cheap \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hogged the spotlight.  \par \par \uc2  In the past two days, both the prime minister and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor have expressed support for a stronger ringgit.  \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday Malaysia further relaxed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules.  \par \par \uc2  But some analysts say that rather than signalling a change in policy, Malaysia is reiterating its tolerance of gradual appreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to limit sharp moves.  \par \par \uc2  "They are now warming up to ringgit strength if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves gradually," said a trader in Kuala Lumpur, referring to the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "What they don't want is a shock to the market."  \par \par \uc2  Still, the latest measures were seen boosting investor sentiment towards the ringgit and paving the way for fresh gains.  \par \par \uc2  "Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures encourage inflows and outflows. But in the current environment they encourage more inflows and this has been endorsed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so the ringgit is staged for further appreciation," said Tan at Bank of America.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  SPOTTING  \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while dealers said the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying dollars for pesos around 48.25 <PHP=>.  \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, traders said that although there was some caution, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  just yet given the momentum behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's rally.  \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has firmed about 0.6 percent in the past two days.  \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/Sing after breaking 1.5240 support should have momentum to 1.5150 and lower," said a trader.  \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is just to smooth the fall.. and I don't think the MAS (\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore) will be too keen to buy U.S. dollars at this level as the Sing dollar is strong on the crosses."  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0754 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.29         117.51       +0.19\par  Sing dlr        1.5163         1.5241       +0.51\par  Taiwan dlr      33.000         33.106       +0.32\par  Korean won      937.10         937.60       +0.05\par  Baht             34.64