\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dollar rises to 9-1/2-year high  \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 21 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose to its highest level in 9-\u189\'00\'BD   years on Wednesday, benefiting from weakness in the U.S. dollar after a report that China would stop amassing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2  It rose as far as 1.5240 to the U.S. dollar, its highest level since October 1997. In late trade on Tuesday it was quoted at 1.5255.  \par \par \uc2  China will stop stockpiling foreign reserves, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Zhou Xiaochuan, said in an interview published on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2  The comments undermined the U.S. dollar in overnight trade although analysts questioned whether China would in practice be able to stop accumulating reserves.  \par \par \uc2   Dealers said wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market could limit gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.  \par \par \uc2  "The China story overnight and selling of the U.S. dollar is driving the Sing dollar," said one trader in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2  "I don't see them (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) in the market, but there were rumours that they were there earlier. If they were there, dollar/Sing would not have come down so fast."  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has also been boosted in the last few days by talk of a possible tightening in Singapore's monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, which is expected to meet in April, sets monetary policy through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead of interest rates. It guides the Singapore dollar within a secret, trade-weighted band. ((Reporting by Dhara Ranasinghe, editing by Alan Raybould; Reuters Messaging: dhara.ranasinghe.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65-6870 3840))   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE-DOLLAR|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070321e33l000p4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
