\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia nudges up with yuan after China rate rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 816 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 04:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 19 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged up against the dollar on Monday, with sentiment slightly bullish after a weekend decision by China to raise interest rates boosted hopes of faster yuan appreciation.  \par \par \uc2  The yuan <CNY=CFXS> touched a post-revaluation high of 7.7330 to the dollar, while China's main stock index <.SSEC> bounced back from early losses to jump nearly 3 percent.  \par \par \uc2  The reaction in Chinese stocks to the rate move was in focus given recent volatility in global markets and its rally, together with gains in other Asian equity markets <.MSCIAPJ>, supported local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  "The Shanghai stock index, and other equity markets in Asia, shrugged off the rate hike. One possible reason for the reaction could be that some in the market inaccurately perceive this as the end of rate hikes in China," said Bank of America \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Christy Tan.  \par \par \uc2  "I doubt the rate move has a significant impact on where the yuan is trading right now, but it is a possible endorsement of further yuan appreciation."  \par \par \uc2  China lifted its benchmark one-year yuan lending and deposit rates by 0.27 percentage point each, taking the one-year deposit rate to 2.79 percent and the lending rate to 6.39 percent.  \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=> gained as much as 0.28 percent to a two-week high at about 942 per dollar, but had trimmed gains by late trade.  \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's ringgit strengthened to about 3.4960 per dollar <MYR=>, its highest in just over two weeks, while in onshore trade in Thailand, the baht <THB=TH> hit 34.79 to the dollar -- its strongest since about September 1997.  \par \par \uc2  "Exporters are still selling the U.S. dollar," said a Bangkok trader. "The trend for the baht is still up."  \par \par \uc2  SPOTLIGHT ON SING DOLLAR  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> gained as much as a quarter of a percent to 1.5248 per U.S. dollar, within sight of Friday's peak of 1.5245 -- the highest in two weeks and a level matching a nine-year high seen in late February and early March. Dealers said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been trading at the weaker end of its band, but since Friday there has been heavy U.S. dollar selling by funds.  \par \par \uc2  They said this was partly triggered by talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) could tighten monetary policy at its next meeting.  \par \par \uc2  The MAS sets monetary policy through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead of interest rates, guiding the Singapore dollar within a trade-weighted band whose parameters are kept secret.  \par \par \uc2  "The Sing NEER (nominal effective exchange rate) has been at the bottom end of the band -- it's actually come down 70 basis points from where it was a month ago," said a Singapore trader.  \par \par \uc2  "So people are just taking this into consideration and maybe also that the MAS might change their policy next month. I doubt this will happen though."  \par \par \uc2  The trader said the market was wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar gains, but added that the MAS had not been spotted in the market on Monday.  \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> fell to a 4-1/2-month low at about 33.15 to the U.S. dollar, continuing to underperform other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  "The Taiwan dollar is being recognised as an attractive funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so when there is carry trade interest floating around, that's where the bias for the Taiwan dollar is as well," said Bank of America's Tan.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0801 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.18         116.87       -0.26\par  Sing dlr        1.5245         1.5286       +0.27\par  Taiwan dlr      33.108         33.102       -0.02\par  Korean won      943.20         944.40       +0.13\par  Baht             34.82          34.90       +0.23\par  Peso             48.72          48.85       +0.28\par  Rupiah         9220.00        9223.00       +0.03\par  Rupee            44.09          44.12       +0.07\par  Ringgit         3.4990         3.5080       +0.26\par  Yuan            7.7370         7.7390       +0.03\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.18         119.01       +1.56\par  Sing dlr        1.5245         1.5337       +0.60\par  Taiwan dlr      33.108         32.585       -1.58\par  Korean won      943.20        0929.50       -1.45\par  Baht             34.82          36.08       +3.62\par  Peso             48.72          49.03       +0.65\par  Rupiah         9220.00        8988.00       -2.52\par  Rupee            44.09          44.26       +0.38\par  Ringgit         3.4990         3.5270       +0.80\par  Yuan            7.7370         7.8051       +0.88\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070322e33j0005a\par }\page {\par\