\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Up On Weak US Dlr Sentiment; Bonds Down  \b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 08:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5287   -0.0041 \par  Overnight Rate         2.75%    +87 bps \par  Two-Year Bond Yield:   2.47%    +4 bps \par  10-Year  Bond Yield:   2.91%    +1 bp \par  Two-Year Swap Offer:   3.06%    +6 bps \par  10-Year  Swap Offer:   3.29%    +5 bps \par  2-10-Year Swap Curve:  23 bps   -1 bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar strengthened in line with broad U.S. dollar weakness in Asian trade Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "The dollar story is slowing beginning to come back. It is coming back into play with the risk aversion story, so next week should be interesting," said Emmanuel Ng, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist from the Overseas Chinese Banking Corp.  \par \par \uc2 He said U.S. dollar weakness has been "the flavor for the day" following weak manufacturing data from New York and Philadelphia Thursday night. The stronger February U.S. producer price index didn't help the greenback, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar-Sing will continue to be heavy (next week), with support first at S$1.5250, then at S$1.5200," Ng said. He doesn't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until it is near S$1.5200.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band as its key monetary policy tool.  \par \par \uc2 Another local bank dealer said the yen carry trade would likely continue to affect the U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar, but he thinks the pair should remain heavy in the long term, due to a strong Singapore economy.  \par \par \uc2 He said the decline in Singapore's February non-oil exports had little effect on the overall health of Singapore's economy.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore bonds market, prices fell, tracking the U.S. Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is stabilizing now, though the rates are still quite soft," said a local bond dealer. "People are trying to figure out what the right levels are."  \par \par \uc2 She said liquidity in the shorter-dated bonds is drying up, as "the value for holding the current yield is way too low," which caused a bigger fall in the price in the shorter-dated bonds Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Overnight rates also spiked on "an outflow of funds, resulting in a lack of liquidity," she said.  \par \par \uc2 "People may buy the belly part of the curve if they need bonds," the dealer said. "However, there's an auction in (the first week of) April for five-year bonds, so response may be mixed."  \par \par \uc2 The five-year bonds traded at 2.73% at 0654 GMT Friday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com [ 16-03-07 0716GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070316e33g000ah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
