2\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the pair falls to S$1.5200. Dealers expect the pair to trade between S$1.5210 and S$1.5350 for the rest of the week. The MAS operates monetary by managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an undisclosed trading band. Singapore government bond prices were higher across the board. 'The bond market is traditionally a safe haven,' said a local bond dealer. 'The key's still the equity market. If equities continue to fall tomorrow, bond prices will continue to rise.' -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070305e335002s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
