\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Up As Regional  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkts Stabilize, Bonds Fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 09:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5278   -0.0022 \par  Overnight rate         2.88%    +38bps \par  Two-year bond yield:   2.91%    +1 bp \par  10-year bond yield:    3.08%    +1 bps \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.40%    +2 bps \par  10-year swap offer:    3.52%    +5 bps \par  2-10-year swap curve:  12bps    +3 bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose slightly in Asian trade Thursday on weak sentiment toward the U.S. dollar and as regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets that were roiled Wednesday were more stable.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Emmanuel Ng, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp., said reduced aversion to risk, a rebound in regional stock markets and reduced liquidation of carry trades between the yen and the long Singapore dollar stabilized the local market.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were shaken Wednesday by a global selloff in stock markets that began in Shanghai on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "If the risk aversion goes away, the pair will head lower," Ng said. "There's still weak dollar sentiment now, keeping the USD/SGD top heavy."  \par \par \uc2 A local bank dealer said bearish sentiment toward the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should see the U.S. unit continue to weaken against the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 He said the pair isn't in danger of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the market "too calm" to warrant any action.  \par \par \uc2 Ng said the Singapore dollar's trade weighted index isn't near the extreme strong end of its trading band and so \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't likely.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS conducts monetary policy by managing the Singapore dollar within an undisclosed policy band. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently has a policy stance of allowing a gradual and modest appreciation of the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the pair to trade in the familiar range between S$1.5260 and S$1.5300 for the rest of the week.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds fell slightly, tracking U.S Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 "There was too much action the past two days, the market is trying to catch its breath now," said a bond dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "The equities market is recovering, so prices for the bonds will fall a little. Overall, it should consolidate after the strong rally."  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com [ 01-03-07 0802GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070301e331000c8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
