\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Up On Weak USD, Traders Expect MAS To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2007\par 08:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5275   -0.0013 \par  Overnight rate         2.56%    -25bp \par  Two-year bond yield:   2.92%    unch \par  10-year bond yield:    3.14%    -5 bp \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.45%    -1 bp \par  10-year swap offer:    3.53%    -2 bp \par  2-10-year swap curve:  8 bps    -1 bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar strengthened slightly in Asian trade Tuesday on continued U.S. dollar weakness against regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but traders expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soon.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is edging quite close to the level where the MAS could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The threshold is about 0.1% to 0.2% from its current level," said Nizam Idris, an analyst at UBS.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think the MAS wants to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly to push it (the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) down. It's too much volatility in the market, and it's not what they usually want to do."  \par \par \uc2 Idris, therefore, predicts that the pair could stay in its current range for a "long, long time".  \par \par \uc2 Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2 Another foreign bank trader said that some dealers are buying the U.S. unit "in anticipation of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " and that they would take profit if the pair reaches S$1.5310.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore longer-dated bonds rose, tracking a rally in the U.S. Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 "The bonds will follow the U.S. market this week," said a local bond dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Bonds had also rallied Monday after the first auction of 20-year Singapore government bonds was at a lower-than-expected yield.  \par \par \uc2 "There's enough supply in the 20-year bond. Traders were just adjusting their positions (yesterday)," the local dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The market is also waiting fourth-quarter U.S. gross domestic product, which will be released Wednesday, and the February ISM Manufacturing Index data, which will be released Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com [ 27-02-07 0744GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070227e32r000ad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
