\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up On US Rate Woes; Bonds Up On 20-Yr Auction  \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2007\par 08:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5288   -0.0046 \par  Overnight rate         2.81%    -7 bp \par  Two-year bond yield:   2.90%    -3 bp \par  10-year bond yield:    3.19%    -5 bp \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.46%    -5 bp \par  10-year swap offer:    3.55%    -8 bp \par  2-10-year swap curve:  9 bps    -3 bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose to its highest level since 1997 Monday after sentiment toward the U.S. dollar turned negative over the weekend on growing concerns that interest rates would rise in Europe but remain frozen - or even decline - in the U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "The (U.S.) dollar sentiment will remain soft (for this week)," said a foreign bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit's strength led many to expect that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is all but inevitable.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is too strong on the trade weighted basis," said the dealer. "But there's still demand for the Singapore dollar, so the MAS will be slowing it down."  \par \par \uc2 The main policy tool of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore is managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2 Another local bank dealer sees the U.S. dollar drifting lower in the coming days because of geopolitical tensions surrounding Iran, which could lead to higher oil prices and draw the U.S. into conflict.  \par \par \uc2 "There's nothing else to watch for, so the market is paying attention to the Iran situation," he said.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Vice President Dick Cheney warned Saturday that "all options" are on the table if Iran continues to defy U.N.-led efforts to end Tehran's nuclear ambitions. This was followed by Iranian President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad's declaration Sunday that Iran would move forward with its nuclear program.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar sank to S$1.5274 intraday, it's lowest level in nine years. Dealers expect the pair to trade between S$1.5250 and S$1.5350 for the rest of the week.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore bond prices rose after the auction of Singapore's first 20-year government bond.  \par \par \uc2 "The traders had oversold last week, so now everyone is very aggressive in catching up," said a local bond dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS sold S$2.5 billion of 20-year bonds at a cutoff yield of 3.50%, a few basis points below market expectations.  \par \par \uc2 The dealer said the market will still need a few days to adjust positions so she expects traders to buy back more bonds in the next few days.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 26-02-07 0757GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070226e32q000ah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
