\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  talk as Philippine peso at 6-year high  \b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2007\par 04:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Feb 20 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso stalled at a six-year high against the dollar in holiday-thinned Asian trade on Tuesday, reined in by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> and Thai baht <THB=> maintained extremely tight ranges, with much of the region still closed for the Lunar New Year holiday.  \par \par \uc2 Markets in China, Hong Kong, Taiwan, Singapore, Malaysia and Vietnam were closed. China and Taiwan are shut for the whole week.  \par \par \uc2 The peso <PHP=> went back up to 48.03 per dollar, a six-year peak it struck on Monday, at which point it had gained one percent in a week.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said dollar bids from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , seen several times in the past week, persisted.  \par \par \uc2 "Dollar/peso should be consolidating at these levels. There are some strong bids coming in at levels below 48.05 which may be from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said one Manila-based trader.  \par \par \uc2 Yet the trader said he would position for further gains in the peso and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Look at the euro's strength. Everyone's coming to the conclusion that we are in a weaker dollar scenario for a few more days," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro hit a six-week peak against the dollar on Tuesday, extending its rally on mounting expectations the Federal Reserve's next move would be to cut interest rates later this year.  \par \par \uc2 A two-day Bank of Japan policy meeting ends on Wednesday and operators remain divided over the chances of a rate rise. That lent little support to the yen <JPY=>, which weakened to near 120 to a dollar.  \par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE GROWTH SURGE?  \par \par \uc2 Fundamental support for the peso seemed to be growing.  \par \par \uc2 An aide to President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo said on Tuesday economic growth might accelerate to seven percent this year from 5.4 percent in 2006, and eventually to a higher rate of 9 percent by 2009.  \par \par \uc2 Strong inflows of remittances from overseas workers and a rally in local stocks have bolstered the peso. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained 2 percent versus the dollar this year, making it Asia's best-performing unit.  \par \par \uc2 "Fundamentally it is a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the risks are mostly cyclical," said UBS \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Nizam Idris.  \par \par \uc2 Structural flows from exports and remittances remained strong and there was low risk of the government compromising on an improving fiscal position by spending more ahead of the May congressional elections, Idris said.  \par \par \uc2 "We could, however, see a slower pace of growth in remittances going forward."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at   0729 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       119.86         121.10       +1.03\par  Korean won      938.30         934.90       -0.36\par  Baht             35.64          35.78       +0.41\par  Peso             48.04          48.39       +0.74\par  Rupiah         9060.00        9041.00       -0.21\par  Rupee            44.17          44.14       -0.08\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f