\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Rises On GDP But Capped By  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Talk  \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2007\par 10:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Latest   Change\par  USD/SGD                1.5392   -0.0043\par  Overnight rate         3.06%    -0.07\par  Two-year bond yield:   2.95%    -1 bp\par  10-year bond yield:    3.23%    +1 bp\par  Two-year swap offer:   3.52%    +1 bp\par  10-year swap offer:    3.62%    -1 bp\par  2-10-year swap curve:  10 bps   unch\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar strengthened in Asian trade Wednesday after the government raised the city-state's 2007 growth forecast, but its upside was limited by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. "I think the only thing hindering the market from selling (the U.S. dollar) is the authorities. They had been rather aggressive (in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) two days ago, so the market will stay pat and wait for the level to stabilize," said an analyst at a research firm who declined to be named. Singapore's economy expanded an annualized 7.9% in the fourth quarter of 2006 from the third, faster than the government's advance estimate of 7.6%, and the 2007 growth target was raised to a range of 4.5%-6.5% from 4%-6%. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the pair reached S$1.5380-S$1.5385. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore operates monetary policy by managing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band. A trader at a foreign bank said the Singapore government's budget, due Thursday, may influence trade because the size of a corporate tax cut and the timing for an increase in the goods and services tax are likely to be announced. The pair is likely to trade between S$1.5350 and S$1.5450 next week, the analyst from the research firm said. "It's a short week next week, so I doubt the pair will move much, unless the dollar-yen creeps lower or Bernanke says something dovish in his speech these two days." Markets in Singapore are closed Monday and Tuesday for the Lunar New Year Holiday. In the Singapore bond market, prices were mostly flat though shorter-dated bonds rose marginally on inflows, a local bond dealer said. "Right now, everyone is just focused on the 20-year auction," the dealer said. "Players are on the sideline, no one wants to make any bets before the 20-year." The size of the 20-year auction is likely to be announced Thursday or Friday. -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070214e32e003xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
