\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr at 1-month low, c.bank's hand suspected  \b0\par\par\uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2007\par 03:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 13 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar hit a one-month low against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday, extending falls on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while a soft tone in equities kept other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the back foot.  \par \par \uc2  A sharp sell-off in the Singapore dollar began overnight when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) was suspected of buying U.S. dollars and dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably in the market again on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> weakened as far as 1.5440 per U.S. dollar, its lowest level since Jan. 12, taking its drop so far this week to about 0.7 percent.  \par \par \uc2  While MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not unusual, dealers said the scale of the latest bout of dollar buying had taken them by surprise.  \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last night was pretty strong, we think it was in the region of $600-700 million," said a trader in Singapore. "We are at a bit of a loss as to why they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Maybe they were trying to pre-empt any fall in dollar/yen."  \par \par \uc2  Another market estimate put the overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as high as $1 billion.  \par \par \uc2  The MAS conducts monetary policy through the exchange rate rather than interest rates, holding the Singapore dollar in an undisclosed band. Its current policy is to pursue "a modest and gradual appreciation" of the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  To some analysts, the MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflected a bid to stop speculators from pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar too high.  \par \par \uc2  "Recent MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been weak and not sufficient to dislodge offshore speculative positions. This time around, their intention has been clearly not just to cap Singapore dollar strength but squeeze out the spec positions," said one analyst.  \par \par \uc2  "They're basically saying enough is enough -- let's be a bit more aggressive now."  \par \par \uc2  Position-covering ahead of Thursday's Singapore budget and next week's Chinese New Year holiday also weighed on the Singapore dollar, another trader said.  \par \par \uc2  EQUITY WEAKNESS  \par \par \uc2  Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were undermined by a sell-off in regional equity markets <.MSCIAPJ> and failed to draw comfort from a rally in the Japanese yen <JPY=>.  \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> dipped to about 33.09 to the U.S. dollar, its lowest level since Nov. 2, as foreign investors dumped Taiwan shares for a second day.  \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=> slipped as much as 0.2 percent to a two-week low at about 939.40 per dollar, while the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> fell a third of a percent to about 9,075 per dollar, its lowest in about a week.  \par \par \uc2  "There has been some dollar buying interest from local banks," said a trader in Jakarta. "Market sentiment is moderately bullish, and we could move to 9,080."  \par \par \uc2  Market attention was turning to this week's main events -- congressional testimony on the U.S. economic outlook from Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke on Wednesday and Thursday and Japanese economic growth data on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2  "We have the Japanese GDP numbers and the Bernanke testimony coming up, so we won't see strong direction in the market for the next 48 hours," said OCBC Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Emmanuel Ng.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0757 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       121.44         121.75       +0.26\par  Sing dlr        1.5421         1.5333       -0.57\par  Taiwan dlr      33.081         33.024       -0.17\par  Korean won      939.40         937.50       -0.20\par  Baht             35.76          35.72       -0.11\par  Peso             48.48          48.37       -0.24\par  Rupiah         9072.00        9043.00       -0.32\par  Rupee            44.16          44.16       +0.01\par  Ringgit         3.5000         3.4930       -0.20\par  Yuan            7.7584         7.7568       -0.02\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       121.44         119.01       -2.00\par  Sing dlr        1.5421         1.5337       -0.54\par  Taiwan dlr      33.081         32.585       -1.50\par  Korean won      939.40        0929.50       -1.05\par  Baht             35.76          36.08       +0.89\par  Peso             48.48          49.03       +1.13\par  Rupiah         9072.00        8988.00       -0.93\par  Rupee            44.16          44.26       +0.23\par  Ringgit         3.5000         3.5270       +0.77\par  Yuan            7.7584         7.8051       +0.60\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070216e32d0004s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pi