\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down On Rumored MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2007\par 08:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5435   +0.0092 \par  Overnight rate         3.13%    +0.22 \par  Two-year bond yield:   2.96%    unch \par  10-year bond yield:    3.22%    +2 bps \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.53%    +1 bp \par  10-year swap offer:    3.63%    +2 bp \par  2-10-year swap curve:  10 bps   +1 bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was weaker in Asian trade Tuesday as traders believed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the European session overnight.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 However, the U.S. dollar is likely to slide in the next few sessions as the Chinese New Year holidays approach, a local bank economist said.  \par \par \uc2 "The Chinese market will be closed, and the offshore (non-deliverable forwards) will push the yuan up and that may put appreciative pressure on the Singapore dollar," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The outlook "will be clearer after the Chinese New Year."  \par \par \uc2 He doesn't expect the MAS to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again and questioned whether MAS did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "I don't see why MAS would want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  though the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is at its toppish side," he said. "The other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are all range-bound."  \par \par \uc2 He expects the pair to trade between S$1.5300 and S$1.5450 for the rest of the week.  \par \par \uc2 One trader said the MAS employed DBS Bank to sell more than S$1 billion to drive the pair from around S$1.5340 to over S$1.5415 in the European session Monday. A DBS spokeswoman declined to comment.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS' main monetary policy tool is managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2 Another local bank dealer dismissed the market interest in the rumors and said, "It doesn't matter. MAS or no MAS, the damage is already done."  \par \par \uc2 Contrary to the economist's view, the local bank dealer predicts that the pair could rise in the near future.  \par \par \uc2 "There will be unwinding of yen crosses and one of them involves the Singapore dollar, so the Sing will fall," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The pair will be well-supported at S$1.5390, the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The dealer said the Singapore budget Thursday would likely be a nonevent for the market.  \par \par \uc2 The government has "already said what they wanted to do" and the market has priced in the effects of a cut in the corporate tax rate and an increase in consumption tax, the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore bond market, there was little movement ahead of the auction of the Singapore government's first 20-year bond, which is expected Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't expect much movement before the auction - what happens after that, it really depends on the issue size. This bond is out of the curve, so no one knows what it is like," said a local bond dealer.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com [ 13-02-07 0738GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070213e32d000cl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
