\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down On Rumored MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2007\par 09:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Latest   Change\par  USD/SGD                1.5435   +0.0092\par  Overnight rate         3.13%    +0.22\par  Two-year bond yield:   2.96%    unch\par  10-year bond yield:    3.22%    +2 bps\par  Two-year swap offer:   3.53%    +1 bp\par  10-year swap offer:    3.63%    +2 bp\par  2-10-year swap curve:  10 bps   +1 bp\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was weaker in Asian trade Tuesday as traders believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the European session overnight. However, the U.S. dollar is likely to slide in the next few sessions as the Chinese New Year holidays approach, a local bank economist said. 'The Chinese market will be closed, and the offshore (non-deliverable forwards) will push the yuan up and that may put appreciative pressure on the Singapore dollar,' he said. The outlook 'will be clearer after the Chinese New Year.' He doesn't expect the MAS to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again and questioned whether MAS did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . 'I don't see why MAS would want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  though the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is at its toppish side,' he said. 'The other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are all range-bound.' He expects the pair to trade between S$1.5300 and S$1.5450 for the rest of the week. One trader said the MAS employed DBS Bank to sell more than S$1 billion to drive the pair from around S$1.5340 to over S$1.5415 in the European session Monday. A DBS spokeswoman declined to comment. The MAS' main monetary policy tool is managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an undisclosed trading band. Another local bank dealer dismissed the market interest in the rumors and said, 'It doesn't matter. MAS or no MAS, the damage is already done.' Contrary to the economist's view, the local bank dealer predicts that the pair could rise in the near future. 'There will be unwinding of yen crosses and one of them involves the Singapore dollar, so the Sing will fall,' he said. The pair will be well-supported at S$1.5390, the dealer said. The dealer said the Singapore budget Thursday would likely be a nonevent for the market. The government has 'already said what they wanted to do' and the market has priced in the effects of a cut in the corporate tax rate and an increase in consumption tax, the dealer said. In the Singapore bond market, there was little movement ahead of the auction of the Singapore government's first 20-year bond, which is expected Friday. 'I don't expect much movement before the auction - what happens after that, it really depends on the issue size. This bond is out of the curve, so no one knows what it is like,' said a local bond dealer. -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070213e32d00336\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
