\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Steady Before G7; Bonds Mixed  \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2007\par 08:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5325   unch \par  Overnight rate         2.94%    unch \par  Two-year bond yield:   2.93%    -4 bps \par  10-year bond yield:    3.16%    -1 bp \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.48%    +2 bps \par  10-year swap offer:    3.57%    +1 bp \par  2-10-year swap curve:  9 bps    -1 bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar remained steady against the greenback Friday as traders wait anxiously to see whether the weekend summit of the Group of Seven major industrial nations results in a strong call for the appreciation of Japanese yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "It's heavy on the USD/SGD at S$1.5300 strong support for the day," said Emmanuel Ng, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for the Overseas Chinese Banking Corp. "If we do get explicit pressure for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, then there would be a top-heavy trend. (The pair)may try again on the downside."  \par \par \uc2 Ng predicts the USD/SGD to range from S$1.5250 to S$1.5400 next week.  \par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at S$1.5280, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar reaches the top end of its undisclosed trading band, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Another foreign bank dealer said he would recommend selling on rally at S$1.5380.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore bonds market, there was a little buying in shorter-dated bonds on fund flows from the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Otherwise, bond trading will remain quiet until the market reopens Feb. 21 after the Chinese New Year holiday, said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The market is still waiting for the auction of the 20-year bond, which will likely take place after the Chinese New Year. Traders remain sidelined because they don't want to take up any position before the size of the 20-year bond is announced.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com [ 09-02-07 0739GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070209e329000r5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
