\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Edges Up On Strong-Yen Sentiment; Bonds Flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2007\par 08:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5320   -0.0006 \par  Overnight rate         2.94%    +13 bps \par  Two-year bond yield:   2.99%    unch \par  10-year bond yield:    3.18%    unch \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.46%    -1 bp \par  10-year swap offer:    3.57%    -1 bp \par  2-10-year swap curve:  11 bps   unch \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was a tad higher in Asian trading Wednesday on expectations of a stronger Japanese yen in coming sessions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 A local bank dealer said the U.S. dollar rose slightly against the Singapore dollar in the morning on buying by an American bank, but the effect was offset by the overall weak sentiment for the greenback ahead of the G7 meeting this weekend.  \par \par \uc2 Although U.S. Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson and various Japanese officials had indicated that the yen issue won't be a major topic at the G7 meeting, German Finance Minister Peer Steinbruck said in an interview with The Wall Street Journal published Wednesday that he would push for a meeting of the G7 to discuss the low value of the yen.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 buzz has boosted the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Suan Teck Kin, an economist at United Overseas Bank, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may decide not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  even if the U.S. dollar-\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar fell to the bottom end of the trading band, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "If the dollar-Sing does not cross the S$1.5300 level, we are quite safe," Suan said. "If it strengthens beyond that level, official action may be expected. But this is difficult to say as authorities may let it run in view of the (G7) event coming up."  \par \par \uc2 The MAS' key monetary policy tool is managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the U.S. dollar to trade between S$1.5300 and S$1.5350 for the rest of the week.  \par \par \uc2 The government bond market remained quiet.  \par \par \uc2 "The past three days' (trade has) been practically nonexistent," said a local bond trader. "In view that Chinese New Year is coming up, the whole of February is burned."  \par \par \uc2 "Everyone is playing a waiting game. Maybe it's calm before a storm," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 She said everyone was anxiously waiting for the auction of the 20-year bond, which will likely fall on Feb. 26.  \par \par \uc2 The dealer predicts that the size of the 20-year bond would be large and would carry attractive yields.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com [ 07-02-07 0730GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070207e327000cd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
