\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Edges Higher Ahead Of Data; Bonds Rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2007\par 09:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5355   -0.0024 \par  Overnight rate         3.19%    -6 bps \par  Two-year bond yield:   3.00%    -2 bps \par  10-year bond yield:    3.18%    -2 bps \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.51%    -1 bps \par  10-year swap offer:    3.60%    -3 bps \par  2-10-year swap curve:  9 bps    -2 bps \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar edged up in Asian trade Wednesday, but looks unlikely to gain further ahead of a host of key events in the U.S. tonight, market participants said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury secretary Henry Paulson testifies before the U.S. Congress later in the day, while the Federal Open Market Committee will decide on interest rates and issue an accompanying statement. Also watched will be the U.S. preliminary fourth-quarter gross domestic product data.  \par \par \uc2 "The market's focus is more on the Paulson testimony," said DBS \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Philip Wee.  \par \par \uc2 There is speculation that Paulson will not only be questioned about the Chinese yuan's value, but also about the recent weakness of the yen versus both the U.S. dollar and euro.  \par \par \uc2 "You will notice that ever since the U.S. dollar crossed Y120, the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' appreciation has stalled," said Wee.  \par \par \uc2 If Paulson signals any sympathy with Europe's discomfort over the yen's weakness ahead of the G7 meeting of finance ministers starting Feb. 9, the yen, the Singapore dollar and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could rise.  \par \par \uc2 Currently the Singapore dollar is still near the top end of its trade-weighted band, according to United Overseas Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "SGD (Singapore dollar) should be capped at 1.5324 level in the extreme case, as it corresponds to the NEER (net effective exchange rate) at 2.5% above the midpoint," said a UOB report, implying this level would be an automatic trigger for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  operates monetary policy by keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore bond market saw yields edge down in muted trade ahead of the FOMC decision.  \par \par \uc2 "Yields have gone up quite significantly in recent sessions so perhaps players are thinking the pendulum has swung too far and decided to reposition before the Fed statement," OCBC fixed income strategist Selena Ling said.  \par \par \uc2 A more hawkish Fed stance in response to recent strong U.S. economic data would likely provoke Singapore bond weakness tomorrow.  \par \par \uc2 Ling said that fears of this were probably overdone and that the Fed is unlikely to adjust its stance significantly.  \par \par \uc2 -By Singapore Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com [ 31-01-07 0839GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070131e31v000l2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
