Bank. "SGD (Singapore dollar) should be capped at 1.5324 level in the extreme case, as it corresponds to the NEER (net effective exchange rate) at 2.5% above the midpoint," said a UOB report, implying this level would be an automatic trigger for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  operates monetary policy by keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band. The Singapore bond market saw yields edge down in muted trade ahead of the FOMC decision. "Yields have gone up quite significantly in recent sessions so perhaps players are thinking the pendulum has swung too far and decided to reposition before the Fed statement," OCBC fixed income strategist Selena Ling said. A more hawkish Fed stance in response to recent strong U.S. economic data would likely provoke Singapore bond weakness tomorrow. Ling said that fears of this were probably overdone and that the Fed is unlikely to adjust its stance significantly. -By Singapore Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070131e31v003xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
