\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Slightly Up In Lackluster Trade; Bonds Inch Dn  \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2007\par 09:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5379   -0.0027 \par  Overnight rate         3.25%    +6 bps \par  Two-year bond yield:   3.02%    +1 bps \par  10-year bond yield:    3.20%    +2 bps \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.52%    +1 bps \par  10-year swap offer:    3.63%    unch \par  2-10-year swap curve:  11 bps   unch \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was slightly higher in Asian trade Tuesday, but market participants say the unit still lacks a catalyst to break out of its recent tight trading range.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "Sideways will still be the catch phrase for the next 24 to 36 hours," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 The sideways trading pattern reflects investor caution ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve interest rate meeting that begins Tuesday, the strategist said.  \par \par \uc2 He added that Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a group were starting to consolidate against the U.S. dollar ahead of the G7 meeting of finance ministers in Germany that starts Feb. 9.  \par \par \uc2 The meeting is likely to discuss the recent weakness of the Japanese yen and could act as a pivot for the value of the yen vs the euro and U.S. dollar, subsequently providing direction for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 He expects solid near-term U.S. dollar support at S$1.5340 - where \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be triggered - and resistance at S$1.5430.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages the local unit within an undisclosed, trade-weighted band, and is suspected of recently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar appreciation.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  unemployment and money supply data due Wednesday are likely to be overshadowed by external factors, according to United Overseas Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect trading to be led by U.S. data releases and developments on the RMB (Chinese Yuan)," UOB said in a report.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds inched lower in quiet trade.  \par \par \uc2 "We are just tracking Treasurys," said a local bond trader. "There's some apprehension that the Fed statement may be more hawkish than previously expected, and that's keeping some players out of the market," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve statement is due around 1800 GMT Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Singapore Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 30-01-07 0813GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070130e31u000fj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
