\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Flat Late, Capital Inflows Offer Support  \b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2007\par 09:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5353   +0.0003 \par  Overnight rate         3.06%    +6 bps \par  Two-year bond yield:   2.98%    -2 bps \par  10-year bond yield:    3.13%    unch \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.47%    unch \par  10-year swap offer:    3.55%    unch \par  2-10-year swap curve:  8 bps    unch \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was almost flat in Asian trade Thursday, but capital inflows continue to exert upward pressure on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders say.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "The Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ex-Japan) are still being driven higher by strong equity-related inflows, and it is difficult to identify possible negative catalysts," a strategist at a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The prospect of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is preventing a breakout of the Singapore dollar from its current range, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls money supply by exchange-rate targeting and manages the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed, trade-weighted band.  \par \par \uc2 At current levels, the Singapore dollar is close to the upper edge of the policy band, according to analyst estimates.  \par \par \uc2 United Overseas Bank estimated in a note that if the greenback fell to S$1.5330, the trade-weighted Singapore dollar would be 2.5% above the midpoint, or at the stronger edge of the policy band.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said the MAS sold the city-state's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight, driving the U.S. dollar up from S$1.5335 to S$1.5380.  \par \par \uc2 Thursday's appreciation of the yen against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar could have lessened the likelihood of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weakened to Y78.37 from around Y78.85 earlier Thursday, easing the local unit away from the top of the band.  \par \par \uc2 A local trader said a decline in the greenback to S$1.5325 could trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said "much depends" on the yen.  \par \par \uc2 He added that the U.S. dollar would need a sustained break below Y120 before the Singapore dollar could continue its trend to the upside.  \par \par \uc2 In the government bond market, limited buying interest supported short-dated maturities, but activity was otherwise "very quiet," a local trader said.  \par \par \uc2 "The only real theme is the expected steepening of the yield curve in advance of the issue of the new 20-year bond," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore is scheduled to issue its first 20-year government bond on Mar. 1.  \par \par \uc2 The next market catalyst may be U.S. existing home sales data expected later Thursday, and players will watch for a possible reaction by U.S. Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 -By Singapore Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 25-01-07 0815GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070125e31p000em\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
