\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia gets a supportive hand from the yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 850 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2007\par 03:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 25 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were largely steady on Thursday, underpinned by a strong recovery in the yen on reports that European officials may complain about yen weakness at a Group of Seven (G7) meeting in February.  \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso <PHP=> was in focus before an interest rate decision, with comments earlier this week from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor dampening expectations for a rate reduction.  \par \par \uc2  Gains in some regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Singapore dollar <SGD=>, South Korean won <KRW=> and Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> were limited by wariness that authorities would or had stepped into the market to cap \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.  \par \par \uc2  Westpac Bank analysts said the market was wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar around the 1.5350 per U.S. dollar area.  \par \par \uc2  In Seoul, the won ended the day around 936 per dollar after what dealers called "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " by the authorities.  \par \par \uc2  South Korean Finance Minister Kwon O-kyu warned on Thursday against excessive dollar/won forward sales by local exporters, which the government has blamed for the won's sharp rise versus the dollar and yen.  \par \par \uc2  "It is interesting to see how central banks in Asia are managing liquidity and encouraging outflows," said Mirza Baig, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2  "That does take pressure off central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2  South Korea said last week it planned to encourage local companies to invest abroad by giving them tax breaks, the latest in a series of efforts to take pressure off the won.  The fortunes of the yen <JPY=>, meanwhile, remained in focus.  \par \par \uc2  Yen carry trades, where investors have sold the low-yielding yen to invest in higher yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helped push the yen to a four-year low versus the dollar earlier this week.  \par \par \uc2  But on Wednesday a short-covering rally that continued after reports about next month's G7 meeting won the yen a reprieve. It traded around 120.40 per dollar, up 0.4 percent from late Wednesday levels.  \par \par \uc2  A PHILIPPINE RATE CUT?  \par \par \uc2  The peso was little moved at about 48.90 per dollar, with attention fixed on this session's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decision.  \par \par \uc2  Expectations that interest rates would be lowered this week were dampened on Monday when Governor Amando Tetangco suggested that a rate cut was not a done deal.  \par \par \uc2  His deputy said on Wednesday that rates could be held steady and a tiering system for overnight rates maintained, but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board would make the final decision.  \par \par \uc2  "Markets are largely expecting no change but will look at the rhetoric from the monetary policy board," a Manila trader said.  \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Thai baht <THB=> edged higher and was quoted at about 35.75 per dollar in the onshore market, compared with about 35.95 on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2  A trader in Bangkok said dollar selling by exporters had pushed the baht up in thin volumes.  \par \par \uc2  "There's also a rumour that maybe the Bank of Thailand will take action soon on the exchange rate -- there is a lot of pressure on it to ease the capital control regulations."  \par \par \uc2  Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveiled capital controls in December, there has essentially been a two-tier market in the baht, with an offshore and an onshore aspect.  \par \par \uc2  Analysts said reports this week that Thailand could take measures to improve trading liquidity in the offshore market and investor-friendly comments from officials have helped sentiment.  \par \par \uc2  "In the last few days the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have sounded more investor friendly," said OCBC \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Emmanuel Ng. "As long as the capital controls remain, a two-tier market will persist."  Change on the day at 0748 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       120.50         120.94       +0.37\par  Sing dlr        1.5347         1.5346       -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr      32.816         32.807       -0.03\par  Korean won      935.80         935.90       +0.01\par  Baht             35.75          35.93       +0.50\par  Peso             48.92          48.84       -0.16\par  Rupiah         9098.00        9076.00       -0.24\par  Rupee            44.23          44.29       +0.14\par  Ringgit         3.5000         3.5000       +0.00\par  Yuan            7.7684         7.7723       +0.05\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       120.50         119.01       -1.24\par  Sing dlr        1.5347         1.5337       -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr      32.816         32.585       -0.70\par  Korean won      935.80        0929.50       -0.67\par  Baht             35.75          36.08       +0.92\par  Peso             48.92          49.03       +0.22\par  Rupiah         9098.00        8988.00       -1.21\par  Rupee    