\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Tad Up Near Top Of Band; Bonds Resilient  \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2007\par 09:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD                1.5350   -0.0026 \par  Overnight rate         3.00%    unch \par  Two-year bond yield:   3.01%    +3 bps \par  10-year bond yield:    3.13%    +2 bps \par  Two-year swap offer:   3.47%    +2 bps \par  10-year swap offer:    3.55%    +3 bps \par  2-10-year swap curve:  8 bps    +1 bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose slightly in Asia Wednesday, but growing concerns of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may restrain further gains, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading near the top of its undisclosed trade-weighted band, within which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its chief policy tool.  \par \par \uc2 One trader said there were "good bids" for the U.S. dollar around S$1.5350, but "no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar could gain further against the greenback if the local unit loses substantial ground against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the trade-weighted basket, especially the Japanese yen.  \par \par \uc2 The yen rose against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Wednesday, as short-sellers exited a carry-trade linked to the Australian dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar weakened to Y78.80 from around Y79.20 late in the day, easing the local unit away from the top the band.  \par \par \uc2 One trader identified S$1.5340 as the nearest crucial support for the greenback, and a break below that could prompt a further short-term drop.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds rose slightly, despite U.S. Treasurys falling overnight.  \par \par \uc2 "The SGS market outperformed today, despite the negative cues from Treasurys and swap rates this morning," said a local market maker. "Buyers emerged early which led to stalemate in the market," she said.  \par \par \uc2 She added that long-dated issues also held up well, as the market is comfortable with the estimated $2.5 billion size of the new 20-year bond auction scheduled for Mar. 1.  \par \par \uc2 -By Singapore Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 24-01-07 0853GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070124e31o000fn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
