\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dlr Gains On 4Q GDP,Regional Strength  \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2007\par 08:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD               1.5292   -0.0041 \par  Overnight rate        3.00%    -75 bps \par  Two-year bond yield:  2.97%    -4 bps \par  10-year bond yield:   3.02%    -3 bps \par  Two-year swap offer:  3.33%    -5 bps \par  10-year swap offer:   3.34%    -6 bps \par  2-10-year swap curve: +1 bp    -1 bp \par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar gained Wednesday in Asia on the first trading day of 2007, reflecting investors' strong appetite for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. 'Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are in demand now,' said one foreign bank dealer. 'It is looking very bright for all the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a lot of hot money is coming in.' 'The U.S economy is slowing down...so, naturally, investors would choose the strong Asian economies, which in turn benefit the Singapore dollar,' he said. The Singapore dollar's appeal was underscored by a government report Wednesday that said gross domestic product grew a seasonally adjusted 7.6% in the fourth quarter from July-September, faster than the third quarter's 5.6% expansion. Thio Chin Loo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas, said Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  look very bright and they will 'start the year very well.' She predicts the U.S. dollar to be supported at S$1.5250 in the near term. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength means there is a risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . 'I don't dismiss MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . MAS is always there to smoothen any market swings,' she said. 'The level of the decline is not so important. Instead, if the pair falls too quickly or it's not in level with the rest of its major trading partners, then MAS would step in.' The MAS operates monetary policy by managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band. The Singapore dollar's gains sparked a rally in the bond market, especially in the shorter-dated bonds. 'We are trading on our own today because of the strong Singapore dollar. After this, we will continue to track the U.S. Treasurys as per normal,' a local bond dealer said. Traders are watching the U.S. December ISM Manufacturing Index and the Federal Open Market Committee Meeting later in the global session. -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires, 65-6415-4036, weiyi.lim@dowjones.com -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070103e313002mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
