\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -S.Korean won down on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , rest follow  \b0\par\par\uc2 753 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2006\par 03:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced the South Korean won to retreat on Friday from the previous session's nine-year high and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell, too, with analysts suspecting a three-week rally was losing steam.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's listlessness against the majors played a part as traders held back ahead of U.S. non-farm payrolls data that could provide fresh pointers to the way Federal Reserve policy is headed.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> straddled 1.54 per U.S. dollar, barely changed from Thursday and less than half a cent away from a nine-year high of 1.5362 struck earlier this week.  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> fell to levels on the weaker side of 920 per dollar, slipping fast from Thursday's high of 912.6.  \par \par \uc2 At those highs, the won had gained 11 percent this year.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the Bank of Korea could have bought up to $1.8 billion.  \par \par \uc2 "Today, it's profit-taking and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mirza Baig, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Deutsche Bank, referring to the won's decline.  \par \par \uc2 The won's rally on Thursday to nine-year highs surprised analysts because it followed a Bank of Korea announcement that the reserve ratio on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits was being raised from later this month.  \par \par \uc2 That measure was seen aimed at curbing foreign funds flowing into Korea, which were partly responsible for pushing up asset prices and the won.  \par \par \uc2 Baig said he was still positive on the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "I expect one to two percent more upside from here regionally but I would be keeping an eye out for positioning getting stretched," he said.  \par \par \uc2 PICKING THE WINNERS  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> was quoted as high as 35.49 per dollar, continuing to hit eight-year highs. The baht has risen in spite of Bank of Thailand measures announced this week to rein the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in.  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> rose, reaching a 3-1/2-month high near 9,040 per dollar in early deals before finding resistance.  \par \par \uc2 But some analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the won and Thai baht, so far leading the rally, would probably lose pace while the laggards caught up.  \par \par \uc2 "I still think dollar/Asia is biased lower, but the market will be a lot more discriminating in which \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  it favours," said Sue Trinh, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with RBC Capital Markets.  \par \par \uc2 "The Korean won should underperform the region, given it is expensive and given increased flexibility of the Asians," she said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts reckon the Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> and Indian rupee <INR=IN> are likely to outperform the region in the weeks ahead, since they have lagged the rally so far.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems those two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are standing out as leading contenders in 2007. In contrast, I expect Sing dollar and the won have had their time in the sun, which is not to say they won't appreciate, but gains will slow on a relative basis," Trinh said.  \par \par \uc2 The ringgit has appreciated 6 percent this year and the rupee less than 1 percent. That compares with a 15 percent gain for the baht and 8.5 percent for the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=>.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at   0749 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.36         114.83       -0.46\par  Sing dlr        1.5408         1.5377       -0.20\par  Taiwan dlr      32.402         32.285       -0.36\par  Korean won      920.00         913.80       -0.67\par  Baht             35.57          35.57       +0.00\par  Peso             49.63          49.42       -0.42\par  Rupiah         9075.00        9095.00       +0.22\par  Rupee            44.70          44.64       -0.13\par  Ringgit         3.5500         3.5410       -0.25\par  Yuan            7.8256         7.8239       -0.02\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.36         117.96       +2.25\par  Sing dlr        1.5408         1.6625       +7.90\par  Taiwan dlr      32.402         32.850       +1.38\par  Korean won      920.00        1011.60       +9.96\par  Baht             35.57          41.11      +15.57\par  Peso             49.63          53.09       +6.97\par  Rupiah         9075.00        9835.00       +8.37\par  Rupee            44.70          45.04       +0.76\par  Ringgit         3.5500         3.7790       +6.45\par  Yuan            7.8256         8.0702       +3.13\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061211e2c80004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
