\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia higher, won shrugs off  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears  \b0\par\par\uc2 702 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2006\par 05:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 6 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended gains against a weak dollar on Wednesday as optimism about the region's economic picture offset worries about official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=>, backed by the yen's <JPY=> gains, jumped 0.9 percent and went as high as 915.9 per dollar, its strongest since October 1997.  \par \par \uc2 It has gained about 10 percent this year.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar slipped towards a four-month low against the yen and inched nearer a 20-month trough versus the euro due to expectations that its interest rate advantage would be eroded further.  \par \par \uc2 "I think it's still a weak dollar story -- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are backed by strong fundamentals are able to catch up," said UBS \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Nizam Idiris. "The won is following the dollar story, but it's not that alarming for the Bank of Korea for now."  \par \par \uc2 The won's strength in recent days has been underpinned by dollar sales by exporters, despite caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Korea.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia's ringgit <MYR=>, which jumped 0.8 percent on Tuesday, rose another 0.4 percent on Wednesday to 3.544 per dollar, its highest level in nearly nine years.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday a leading Malaysian think tank predicted it could rise to 3.5 in the first quarter of 2007 and called for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to loosen its grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was depegged from the dollar in July 2005.  \par \par \uc2 It has gained about 6.7 percent so far this year but has underperformed other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Singapore dollar, South Korean won, Indonesian rupiah and Thai baht.  \par \par \uc2 FUNDAMENTALS MATTER  \par \par \uc2 A renewed rally in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks has sparked a wave of verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by regional central banks to curb their strength to protect exporters.  \par \par \uc2 "The symptoms of excessive liquidity remain, with regional bonds and equities rallying and showing an increasing mistrust of the dollar, despite all the policy makers' attempts to cajole the market into buying the dollar," Claudio Piron and Yen Ping Ho at JPMorgan said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 Sustained foreign capital flows into the region's equity markets and solid economic fundamentals, including large trade surpluses, are providing support for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite worries over a possible slowdown in the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=>, which took a hit on Monday when the Bank of Thailand announced measures to tighten \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules, rose a quarter of a percent on Wednesday, while the Indonesian rupiah traded between 9,094 and 9,115 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose as high as 1.5362 per U.S. dollar, its strongest level in more than nine years, while the Philippine peso <PHP=> rose to around 49.50 per dollar. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0751 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest b