ar \uc2 On Wednesday, the U.S. dollar fell to an intraday low against the ringgit of MYR3.5380, the lowest since March 1998.  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, bond prices fell, especially in shorter-dated bonds, flattening the curve.  \par \par \uc2 "It's the year-end, people are going on leave so they are just clearing their positions," said a local dealer. "The liquidity in the short-end is very soft, so it actually doesn't make much sense to sell it."  \par \par \uc2 "Traders, however, are holding back on selling the long-end," she said. "They are unsure what is going to happen. If the U.S. declares a spike in interest rates, they will start selling the longer-dated bonds."  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 06-12-06 0751GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061206e2c6000ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
