ort-term bonds were in demand to replace the one-year treasury bill that matured on Nov. 30.  \par \par \uc2 "All the bond yields have broken the 3% threshold, so the market will have to wait if they want a better yield," one local bond dealer said. "If there's better U.S. data this week, the market may use it as an excuse for a retracement, and the yields may trade above the 3.4 percent level."  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 04-12-06 0719GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061204e2c4000bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
