\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Down After MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2006\par 08:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                        Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD               1.5430   +0.0004 \par  Overnight rate        3.13%    +13 bps \par  Two-year bond yield:  2.94%    -3 bps \par  10-year bond yield:   3.00%    -2 bps \par  Two-year swap offer:  3.37%    -4 bps \par  10-year swap offer:   3.32%    -4 bps \par  2-10-yr swap curve:   -5 bps   unch \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar ended slightly lower Friday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  apparently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to erase the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's early gains, and analysts said the local authority may remain active in days ahead.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to keep the market guessing," said a local trader.  \par \par \uc2 Traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, which advocates a modest and gradual appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday and Friday to dampen volatility and to keep the unit within an undisclosed, trade-weighted band.  \par \par \uc2 One bank estimated that the trade-weighted Singapore dollar has weakened in the last two days, largely due to strength in basket \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  other than the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 As a result, there is some scope for the U.S. dollar to continue its decline without lifting the trade-weighted Singapore dollar beyond the policy band limit, a strategist said.  \par \par \uc2 However, the net effective exchange rate is still in the upper half of the MAS' target range, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains possible, the strategist said.  \par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to minimize drastic fluctuations in the U.S. dollar-\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar exchange rate, even if its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  have only short-term effects.  \par \par \uc2 "There are actually two considerations," the strategist said. "The second is the volatility of the spot rate itself."  \par \par \uc2 Last week and on Thursday, the MAS bought U.S. dollars to weaken the Singapore dollar, but the rise in the spot rate retraced within hours.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, traders said the MAS bid the U.S. dollar up to around to S$1.5470 from about S$1.5370, but the greenback eased back to S$1.5430 by 0600 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 In the debt market, government bond prices rose following a weaker-than-expected November manufacturing report in the U.S. that sent Treasury prices higher.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore government bond yield curve steepened slightly, and some investment banks are predicting the two- to 10-year spread to rise by more than 30 basis points by the end of 2007.  \par \par \uc2 "If you look to the U.S., we may be entering a period of monetary easing, and the yield curve should get steeper," said Lee Wee-Kok, a strategist at Standard Chartered. "In Singapore it will be comparable."  \par \par \uc2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4152; john.jannarone@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 01-12-06 0741GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061201e2c1000ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picsc